{% doc %}
  Shows the collector card at the top of the media column, for the Tee of the
  Week only.

  WHY IT IS NOT THE PRODUCT IMAGE. The obvious version of this is to add the
  rendered card to the product's media in Shopify so it simply becomes the first
  photo. That would also push it into the Google and Meta feeds — and Merchant
  Center prohibits promotional overlays on product images. The card has "15% OFF
  ALL WEEK" and a struck price burned into it, so making it product media would
  inject a policy violation into the feed of an account that has already been
  suspended once for misrepresentation.

  So it renders here, on the page, and never enters the catalogue.

  THE URL COMES FROM A PRODUCT METAFIELD, not the tee_week metaobject. That
  metaobject is `storefront: NONE` and opening it up would expose the whole
  queue — including which tees are coming in later weeks. `enrich.tee_card_url`
  carries only the current card, attached to the product it belongs to.

  GUARDED TWICE. The metafield must be present AND the product must still be the
  first in the tee-of-the-week collection. A metafield left behind after a
  rotation would otherwise show last week's card above this week's tee, which is
  worse than showing no card at all.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign card = product.metafields.enrich.tee_card_url.value
  assign is_current = false
  if card != blank
    assign tee_collection = collections['tee-of-the-week']
    if tee_collection != blank and tee_collection.products.first.id == product.id
      assign is_current = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if is_current -%}
  <figure class="aj-teecard">
    <img
      src="{{ card }}"
      alt="Tee of the Week collector card for {{ product.title | escape }}"
      width="1080"
      height="1350"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      class="aj-teecard__img"
    >
  </figure>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    Sits above the gallery rather than replacing it. Someone deciding whether to
    buy a t-shirt still wants the supplier's photographs — the card is the
    framing, the photos are the evidence.

    fetchpriority high and loading eager because this is now the largest element
    in the viewport on this page, and lazy-loading your own LCP image is a
    self-inflicted wound.
  */
  .aj-teecard {
    margin: 0 0 var(--padding-md, 1rem);
  }

  .aj-teecard__img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--aj-cats-radius, 8px);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
